00:24:18,161 --> 00:24:23,160
A laser stands for light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation,

419
00:24:23,161 --> 00:24:30,160
which is a complicated way of saying that they're atomic processes that cause light to be emitted

420
00:24:30,161 --> 00:24:33,160
in a way that all of the light waves move together.

421
00:24:33,161 --> 00:24:38,160
In a laser, there's an interaction between the atoms and the light.

422
00:24:38,161 --> 00:24:43,160
Rather than this light being completely random, going off in all directions and having all colors,

423
00:24:43,161 --> 00:24:50,160
photons in a laser can group up and that will give you this beam which will have these special properties.

424
00:24:50,161 --> 00:24:57,160
But in spite of their visual similarity, a laser beam can't come close to doing the kind of tricks a lightsaber can.

425
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:04,160
They crash into each other and clang. Of course light doesn't do that.

