Believe it or not, Earth scientists are developing just such a defensive technology.

498
00:29:13,961 --> 00:29:16,100
Open fire.

499
00:29:16,101 --> 00:29:20,200
But it'll be a while before they can make a shield tough enough to withstand a blast

500
00:29:20,201 --> 00:29:23,800
at point-blank range.

501
00:29:23,801 --> 00:29:26,160
could potentially be used as a shield.

502
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:30,560
There's scientists now who's developing cold plasmas

503
00:29:30,561 --> 00:29:32,260
because if you had a hot plasma

504
00:29:32,261 --> 00:29:34,580
and you put it around the outside of your ship as a shield,

505
00:29:35,180 --> 00:29:36,580
it would tend to melt your ship.

506
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,940
But if it was a cold plasma,

507
00:29:39,180 --> 00:29:41,160
it could potentially protect your ship.

508
00:29:41,220 --> 00:29:43,300
It could deflect microwaves.

509
00:29:43,301 --> 00:29:46,340
It could potentially deflect laser beams.

510
00:29:46,800 --> 00:29:48,260
They're doing this now

511
00:29:48,261 --> 00:29:51,200
to potentially shield satellites in orbit.

512
00:29:51,201 --> 00:29:53,700
In the world of Star Wars technology,

513
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:57,200
it's possible for entire planets to have defense shields.

514
00:29:57,300 --> 00:30:01,340
But even they're no match for the deadliest of all Star Wars weapons,

515
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:03,440
the Death Star super laser.

516
00:30:04,740 --> 00:30:07,960
The way the laser works can be compared to a magnifying glass

517
00:30:08,060 --> 00:30:09,660
when held under the sun.

518
00:30:09,760 --> 00:30:12,460
Both devices collect energy and intensify it

519
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,860
into a single searing beam of light.

520
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:19,660
When the Death Star's light beams come together

521
00:30:19,661 --> 00:30:22,160
to make the superlaser, in reality,

522
00:30:22,161 --> 00:30:24,960
those laser beams would just pass right through each other.

523
00:30:24,961 --> 00:30:26,460
They wouldn't combine.

524
00:30:26,461 --> 00:30:29,460
You can focus a single beam of light with a magnifying glass,

525
00:30:29,461 --> 00:30:31,300
but in the way the Death Star does it,

526
00:30:31,301 --> 00:30:33,500
it happens in empty space.

527
00:30:33,501 --> 00:30:35,500
That is, lasers come together

528
00:30:35,501 --> 00:30:37,220
and then go a different direction.

529
00:30:37,221 --> 00:30:40,620
And without some object there to redirect the laser beams,

530
00:30:40,621 --> 00:30:42,420
there's no way that could happen.

531
00:30:42,421 --> 00:30:44,560
We didn't actually have a lens out there.

532
00:30:44,561 --> 00:30:47,020
George talked about how there would be a condenser

533
00:30:47,021 --> 00:30:49,260
of some kind or other, even though it would be invisible,

534
00:30:49,261 --> 00:30:52,540
that would bring multiple laser bolts together

535
00:30:52,541 --> 00:30:55,320
and be able to shoot at an object.

536
00:30:55,600 --> 00:30:58,320
I have chosen to test this station's destructive power

537
00:30:58,321 --> 00:31:00,240
on your home planet of Alderaan.

538
00:31:00,520 --> 00:31:01,220
No.

539
00:31:01,221 --> 00:31:02,340
Commit primary action.

540
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:06,000
So, once again, the Empire's R&D department

541
00:31:06,001 --> 00:31:09,380
seems to be light years ahead of anything we have on Earth,

542
00:31:09,740 --> 00:31:13,300
especially since our scientists have yet to invent a weapon

543
00:31:13,301 --> 00:31:17,040
powerful enough to blow away a planet with a single blast.

544
00:31:19,260 --> 00:31:24,260
But not all Star Wars technology is so deadly.

545
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:27,260
Sometimes it can be downright fun,

546
00:31:27,300 --> 00:31:30,280
especially if you have to travel across deserts

547
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:32,780
or through forests and cities

548
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:36,280
at lightning Tatooine to Endur.

549
00:31:39,380 --> 00:31:42,280
And from Coruscant to Naboo,

550
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:47,260
the need for speed seems just as essential

551
00:31:47,261 --> 00:31:50,460
just as essential to the life forms of Star Wars

552
00:31:50,461 --> 00:31:53,060
as it is for thrill-seeking motorcyclists

553
00:31:53,061 --> 00:31:55,140
and race car drivers here on Earth.

554
00:31:56,860 --> 00:31:59,640
Not only are the planetary vehicles of Star Wars

555
00:31:59,641 --> 00:32:01,300
incredible to look at,

556
00:32:01,301 --> 00:32:03,340
they also come fully equipped

557
00:32:03,341 --> 00:32:05,640
with more technological innovations

558
00:32:05,641 --> 00:32:07,480
than you can shake a lightsaber at.

559
00:32:07,481 --> 00:32:10,220
I don't mind flying, but what you're doing is suicide.

560
00:32:13,420 --> 00:32:16,720
Let's take Luke Skywalker's Landspeeder, for example.

561
00:32:16,721 --> 00:32:20,220
George Lucas described it as an auto-like transport

562
00:32:20,221 --> 00:32:25,220
that travels a few feet above the ground on a magnetic field.

563
00:32:25,221 --> 00:32:30,060
Magnetic levitation, or maglev technology, actually exists

564
00:32:30,061 --> 00:32:33,480
and is based on the fact that two like magnetic poles

565
00:32:33,481 --> 00:32:36,180
repel one another.

566
00:32:36,181 --> 00:32:39,140
Maglev trains use this principle and operate

567
00:32:39,141 --> 00:32:42,320
by moving a magnet attached to the train.

568
00:32:42,321 --> 00:32:44,680
The action generates a magnetic field,

569
00:32:44,681 --> 00:32:48,620
which lifts and propels the vehicle down the tracks on a cushion of air.

570
00:32:49,700 --> 00:32:54,620
But how would maglev technology work on Luke's home planet, Tatooine,

571
00:32:54,980 --> 00:32:56,860
where there don't appear to be any tracks?

572
00:32:57,360 --> 00:33:00,620
You could do that if the planet's made out of the right magnetic materials,

573
00:33:00,940 --> 00:33:04,540
something like iron or nickel that have a strong magnetic response.

574
00:33:04,980 --> 00:33:06,820
Your ship could generate a magnetic field

575
00:33:06,821 --> 00:33:09,460
that would then cause you to lift above that material.

576
00:33:10,340 --> 00:33:14,600
But what if a planet didn't have the apparent magnetic properties of Tatooine?

577
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:17,180
A place like Coruscant, for instance.

578
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:21,920
How do the airspeeders of that world fly through the sky without wings?

579
00:33:22,520 --> 00:33:26,900
Since these things seem to zip around just about any place and at any altitude you want,

580
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:32,240
it would require something that we don't have yet, pretty much anti-gravity.

581
00:33:32,900 --> 00:33:37,260
We know about magnetism, charged particles attract and repel.

582
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:40,080
So one might think I could get gravity to repel.

583
00:33:40,081 --> 00:33:44,280
It turns out within our universe we know that you can't make gravity repulsive.

584
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:48,340
However, you can look at theories of physics that are consistent within themselves

585
00:33:48,341 --> 00:33:51,560
and could contain other forces that would act like anti-gravity.

586
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:55,680
You can imagine in a completely different universe,

587
00:33:56,040 --> 00:33:59,140
you might get a force that can be repulsive relative to gravity,

588
00:33:59,540 --> 00:34:03,880
and then you can imagine using that as a technology to generate these things that float.

589
00:34:04,420 --> 00:34:08,920
In the Star Wars universe, many vehicles use this notion of anti-gravity.

590
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:12,160
George Lucas called it repulsor lift technology,

591
00:34:12,161 --> 00:34:15,400
which allows crafts of every kind to lift off the ground,

592
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:19,640
hover, and even sail through the sky.

593
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:21,740
It seems like in the Star Wars universe,

594
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:24,040
they have the power to manipulate gravity.

595
00:34:24,620 --> 00:34:26,280
If they can control gravity,

596
00:34:26,920 --> 00:34:31,360
they can make repulsor lift vehicles of any kind.

597
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:33,940
Using repulsor lift technology

598
00:34:33,941 --> 00:34:36,280
to fly above a planet's surface is one thing.

599
00:34:36,700 --> 00:34:39,160
But just how do Luke, Leia, and those nasty stormtroopers

600
00:34:39,161 --> 00:34:44,100
stormtroopers zip through giant redwoods on the moon of Endor without ever hitting a tree?

601
00:34:46,180 --> 00:34:47,680
Well, almost never.

602
00:34:47,681 --> 00:34:53,680
According to Star Wars experts, the answer to why stormtroopers are so quick

603
00:34:53,681 --> 00:34:57,216
can be found right under their high-tech helmets.

604
00:34:57,217 --> 00:35:00,680
I was reading an article recently about guys who

605
00:35:00,681 --> 00:35:02,380
race on motorcycles.

606
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:11,020
And they want helmets that are going to give them GPS data

607
00:35:11,021 --> 00:35:16,160
and data about the track ahead so that they

608
00:35:16,161 --> 00:35:17,640
can react more quickly.

609
00:35:22,200 --> 00:35:25,180
And I got the same thing going on on the moon of Endor

610
00:35:25,181 --> 00:35:27,240
with those speeder bikes.

611
00:35:27,241 --> 00:35:29,580
The stormtroopers weren't terribly bright.

612
00:35:30,680 --> 00:35:36,480
So they did have these helmet systems that helped them to guide the speeder bikes.

613
00:35:38,600 --> 00:35:40,040
They still lost out.

614
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:42,500
The Stormtroopers still crashed into things.

615
00:35:43,920 --> 00:35:49,280
GPS-style helmets would also come in handy when piloting this high-speed Star Wars vehicle,

616
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:54,580
one which uses a technology that can already be found right here on Earth, the Podracer.

617
00:35:54,581 --> 00:35:57,580
As built by young Anakin Skywalker,

618
00:35:57,581 --> 00:36:00,580
the Podracer appears to have Earth-style jet engines.

619
00:36:00,581 --> 00:36:04,580
George described the Podracers as being like two 747 engines

620
00:36:04,581 --> 00:36:06,580
with the exterior covers pulled off,

621
00:36:06,581 --> 00:36:09,580
with this little pod behind it on these wires.

622
00:36:09,581 --> 00:36:11,580
He talked for probably 20 minutes,

623
00:36:11,581 --> 00:36:13,580
right off the top of his head, about the Podracer

624
00:36:13,581 --> 00:36:15,580
and about how it all worked.

625
00:36:18,580 --> 00:36:22,580
And the impression I got was that he was there yesterday at the races.

626
00:36:22,581 --> 00:36:27,580
I remember trying to talk to George about the technology of those huge engines.

627
00:36:30,580 --> 00:36:36,580
Are they really like taking two 747 engines, putting some repulsors so they stay off the ground,

628
00:36:36,581 --> 00:36:39,580
and then binding them together with this electrical beam?

629
00:36:39,581 --> 00:36:42,580
And George's answer was, yeah, that's what it's like.

630
00:36:42,581 --> 00:36:45,580
I asked about the beam in the middle, and he said,

631
00:36:45,581 --> 00:36:49,580
well, the reason is because they've got this centrifugal force going on,

632
00:36:49,581 --> 00:36:54,200
on, this gyroscope going on, and if they weren't bound together like that, they'd actually

633
00:36:54,201 --> 00:36:58,580
smash into each other or head off like two magnets repelling each other.

634
00:36:58,581 --> 00:37:05,500
Ooh, there goes Quadranero's power coupling.

635
00:37:05,501 --> 00:37:11,980
Of course, as far as the forces of evil are concerned, speed isn't everything.

636
00:37:11,981 --> 00:37:15,980
ADATs, better known as Imperial Walkers,

637
00:37:16,020 --> 00:37:18,980
are a terrifying triumph of Empire engineering.

638
00:37:19,020 --> 00:37:21,980
But even though they can trample the heroic rebels

639
00:37:22,020 --> 00:37:24,960
on the planet Hoth as they do in Episode 5,

640
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:26,960
The Empire Strikes Back,

641
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:29,960
these behemoths aren't known for their quick moves.

642
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:32,960
When you look at these large, four-legged pieces of equipment,

643
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:34,980
it's hard to think of situations where they're a huge advantage

644
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:37,980
over a wheeled vehicle because they would be, I think,

645
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:39,980
a lot slower and a little more unstable.

646
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,980
Detach cable!

647
00:37:41,981 --> 00:37:55,680
Fortunately for Empire engineers, their two-legged terrain vehicles, also known as chicken walkers,

648
00:37:55,860 --> 00:37:59,960
were much more practical, even if they were a little unsteady on their feet.

649
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:03,260
That one made a little more sense to me because it's walking around in the jungle,

650
00:38:03,460 --> 00:38:08,980
and you could imagine that you would need something like that in a dense jungle to move more like an animal or a person.

651
00:38:08,981 --> 00:38:14,280
But sometimes the most sophisticated technology is still no match

652
00:38:14,281 --> 00:38:19,240
when pitted against one simple adversary, human ingenuity.

653
00:38:20,460 --> 00:38:22,480
Because as the old saying goes,

654
00:38:22,940 --> 00:38:27,540
the bigger they are, the harder they fall.

655
00:38:30,060 --> 00:38:33,160
I am C3PO, human-cyborg relations,

656
00:38:33,500 --> 00:38:35,580
and this is my counterpart, Barton Dieter.

657
00:38:35,700 --> 00:38:36,400
Hello.

658
00:38:38,980 --> 00:38:43,980
Since 1977, when the first Star Wars film premiered...

659
00:38:43,981 --> 00:38:45,980
Don't get technical with me.

660
00:38:45,981 --> 00:38:48,980
Scientists and engineers have made great strides

661
00:38:48,981 --> 00:38:52,980
toward developing real robots that can execute many of the functions

662
00:38:52,981 --> 00:38:54,980
performed by the droids in Star Wars.

663
00:38:54,981 --> 00:38:55,980
We need to operate quickly.

664
00:38:55,981 --> 00:38:58,980
Using robots to aid in surgery is a very real possibility.

665
00:38:58,981 --> 00:39:02,980
One example would be telesurgery, where a skilled surgeon moves his hand,

666
00:39:02,981 --> 00:39:06,980
and at a distance, a robotic arm imitates his very movement.

667
00:39:06,981 --> 00:39:11,980
Robots are also wonderful for very small precision surgical work as well as repetitive tasks.

668
00:39:11,981 --> 00:39:18,980
Incredibly, robots are even learning how to express emotions, just like C-3PO.

669
00:39:18,981 --> 00:39:22,980
I don't know what all this trouble is about, but I'm sure it must be your fault.

670
00:39:22,981 --> 00:39:24,980
You watch your language.

671
00:39:24,981 --> 00:39:30,980
One area I think Star Wars was a real breakthrough was with the treatment of the droids,

672
00:39:30,981 --> 00:39:33,980
and the fact that the droids have personalities and emotions.

673
00:39:33,981 --> 00:39:38,997
emotions. We seem to be made to suffer. It's our lot in life.

674
00:39:38,998 --> 00:39:42,040
R2 and 3PO, here were two robots with

675
00:39:42,041 --> 00:39:43,993
personalities with lots of emotions.

676
00:39:43,994 --> 00:39:47,140
And don't let me catch you following me, begging for help,

677
00:39:47,240 --> 00:39:52,549
because you won't get it. And these emotions actually helped them.

678
00:39:52,550 --> 00:39:54,480
R2, can you hear me? You

679
00:39:54,481 --> 00:39:58,676
must repair him. Sir, if any of my circuits or gears will help, I'll gladly donate.

680
00:39:58,677 --> 00:39:59,377
He'll be

681
00:39:59,378 --> 00:40:01,080
Emotions help us set priorities.

682
00:40:01,081 --> 00:40:03,080
See if they've been captured. Hurry.

683
00:40:03,081 --> 00:40:06,080
They help us plan and make decisions.

684
00:40:06,081 --> 00:40:10,080
What does that mean? That means I am in charge here.

685
00:40:10,081 --> 00:40:13,080
Researchers are making great progress in building robots

686
00:40:13,081 --> 00:40:15,080
that can emulate human emotions.

687
00:40:15,081 --> 00:40:19,080
As an example, MIT Media Lab's Kismet actually can carry on a conversation with you

688
00:40:19,081 --> 00:40:22,080
and make facial expressions based on your mood.

689
00:40:22,081 --> 00:40:26,080
They've programmed the responses in there so it will respond to your facial clues

690
00:40:26,081 --> 00:40:28,080
using motors and gadgets.

691
00:40:28,081 --> 00:40:30,080
Don't go.

692
00:40:30,081 --> 00:40:32,080
No, I'm not going to go.

693
00:40:32,081 --> 00:40:34,080
Oh, yay.

694
00:40:34,081 --> 00:40:36,080
You're so silly.

695
00:40:36,081 --> 00:40:41,080
The emotions that have been programmed into the robot have been modeled, computationally

696
00:40:41,081 --> 00:40:44,080
modeled, after what we know about human emotions.

697
00:40:44,081 --> 00:40:46,080
I love you.

698
00:40:46,081 --> 00:40:49,080
Aw, did he say he loves me?

699
00:40:49,081 --> 00:40:51,080
I love you.

700
00:40:51,081 --> 00:40:54,080
Humans are super social.

701
00:40:54,081 --> 00:40:56,080
And your favorite color, blue.

702
00:40:56,081 --> 00:40:56,781
No.

703
00:40:57,060 --> 00:41:01,560
So if we want to build a robot that can interact with people,

704
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:03,800
communicate with people, and learn from people,

705
00:41:03,980 --> 00:41:08,420
it has to also be social,

706
00:41:08,740 --> 00:41:11,180
because that's the way that people are going to try to teach it

707
00:41:11,181 --> 00:41:13,000
and the way they're going to try to communicate to it.

708
00:41:13,060 --> 00:41:16,180
No, you're not to do that. No.

709
00:41:17,300 --> 00:41:19,780
R2, that way.

710
00:41:19,781 --> 00:41:27,540
But if robot technology is now taking big steps forward...

711
00:41:27,541 --> 00:41:29,480
What's going on, buddy?

712
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:34,720
Another seemingly simple Star Wars concept is scientifically tougher to crack.

713
00:41:34,860 --> 00:41:35,560
Put him in.

714
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:37,720
Carbonite freezing.

715
00:41:43,400 --> 00:41:45,980
Carbonite really does exist here on Earth.

716
00:41:46,540 --> 00:41:48,200
It's a type of gunpowder.

717
00:41:48,201 --> 00:41:50,040
But it doesn't have the same properties

718
00:41:50,140 --> 00:41:52,980
that it does in the world of Star Wars.

719
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:54,900
The way it's used in the film,

720
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:57,080
it's kind of a dry ice with an opposite charge.

721
00:41:57,180 --> 00:41:59,480
Anything with ite, carbon ite, it means it's

722
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:01,180
some alloy of some mineral.

723
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:05,420
So it's probably some carbon dioxide mineral alloy that

724
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:08,520
is able to be kept at very, very low temperatures.

725
00:42:08,620 --> 00:42:10,660
Well, it's not ever explicitly explained.

726
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:12,820
But even though we haven't yet mastered

727
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:16,260
the art of freezing and unfreezing human beings,

728
00:42:16,261 --> 00:42:18,260
Scientists are working on it.

729
00:42:18,261 --> 00:42:21,260
It's a field of research called cryonics.

730
00:42:21,261 --> 00:42:24,260
Cryonics is a way of taking a tissue

731
00:42:24,261 --> 00:42:27,260
and bringing it down to a very, very low temperature,

732
00:42:27,261 --> 00:42:30,260
so there's no more need for oxygen or blood flow.

733
00:42:30,261 --> 00:42:33,260
And so what you have to do is replace the blood with glycerol.

734
00:42:33,261 --> 00:42:35,260
It's the same stuff we use in the lab

735
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:37,260
to cryogenically preserve tissue.

736
00:42:39,260 --> 00:42:41,260
So you can get organisms, you can get tissue down,

737
00:42:41,261 --> 00:42:42,260
you can get a human down.

738
00:42:42,261 --> 00:42:44,260
The problem is bringing them back up.

739
00:42:44,261 --> 00:42:50,300
If you're warmed up too fast, you fall apart like peanut brittle, and then you just turn

740
00:42:50,301 --> 00:42:51,300
into goo.

741
00:42:51,301 --> 00:42:56,220
You have hibernation sickness.

742
00:42:56,221 --> 00:42:59,420
There's probably good science with the freezing of Han.

743
00:42:59,421 --> 00:43:01,200
The thawing, not so much.

744
00:43:01,201 --> 00:43:02,200
I'm out of it.

745
00:43:02,201 --> 00:43:08,200
